<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= appInfo.name %></title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: linear-gradient(135deg, #efe6dd 0%, #d9ecf0 100%);
            --panel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
            --border: #d7c6ba;
            --accent: #0c7489;
            --accent-soft: #dbf0f5;
            --text: #24313a;
            --muted: #62707a;
        }

        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            min-height: 100vh;
        }
        a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
        .page {
            width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 32px));
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 32px 0 48px;
        }
        .hero, .panel {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 28px;
            padding: 26px;
            box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        }
        .hero-top, .actions, .nav {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 12px;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: flex-start;
        }
        .nav {
            justify-content: flex-start;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        .pill, .link-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 42px;
            padding: 0 14px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
        }
        .pill {
            background: var(--accent-soft);
            color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
            font-size: 0.84rem;
        }
        .link-btn.current, .link-btn.primary {
            background: var(--accent);
            color: white;
            border-color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700;
        }
        .grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
            gap: 18px;
            margin-top: 22px;
        }
        .kpis {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
            gap: 12px;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        .kpi {
            padding: 14px;
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
            border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
        }
        .kpi strong {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 6px;
            font-size: 0.82rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        }
        .mono {
            font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
            font-size: 0.94rem;
            word-break: break-word;
        }
        .error {
            margin-top: 16px;
            padding: 16px 18px;
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: #fff0ec;
            border: 1px solid #e7b6a8;
            color: #8a2b12;
        }
        p, li { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
        pre {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 18px;
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: #172026;
            color: #f1f5f9;
            overflow: auto;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <section class="hero">
            <div class="hero-top">
                <div>
                    <span class="pill">Custom Login Entry</span>
                    <h1>Bring your own page without losing SSO</h1>
                    <p>This demo keeps a branded local <span class="mono">/login</span> page, but the actual sign-in still happens through Cognito Hosted UI. That preserves the Cognito browser session and keeps SSO compatible with <span class="mono">app1</span> and <span class="mono">app2</span>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="actions">
                    <% if (isAuthenticated) { %>
                        <a class="link-btn primary" href="/logout">Logout</a>
                    <% } else { %>
                        <a class="link-btn primary" href="/login">Open Custom Login Page</a>
                    <% } %>
                </div>
            </div>

            <nav class="nav" aria-label="Route switcher">
                <% pageLinks.forEach((link) => { %>
                    <a class="link-btn <%= link.current ? 'current' : '' %>" href="<%= link.href %>"><%= link.label %></a>
                <% }) %>
            </nav>

            <% if (error) { %>
                <div class="error">
                    <strong>Application error</strong>
                    <div class="mono"><%= error %></div>
                </div>
            <% } %>
        </section>

        <section class="grid">
            <article class="panel">
                <h2>Runtime configuration</h2>
                <div class="kpis">
                    <div class="kpi">
                        <strong>Base URL</strong>
                        <div class="mono"><%= appInfo.baseUrl %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi">
                        <strong>Callback URL</strong>
                        <div class="mono"><%= appInfo.redirectUri %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi">
                        <strong>Client ID</strong>
                        <div class="mono"><%= appInfo.clientId %></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi">
                        <strong>Issuer</strong>
                        <div class="mono"><%= appInfo.issuer %></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p>This app expects a normal Cognito Hosted UI and authorization-code setup. The difference is only that your own page starts the browser redirect, instead of dropping users into Cognito immediately.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="panel">
                <h2>What changes compared to App 1 and App 2</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>You keep your own branded entry page at <span class="mono">/login</span>.</li>
                    <li>The app can pass a username hint before the redirect to Cognito.</li>
                    <li>Cognito still handles the credential page, MFA, and browser session.</li>
                    <li>Because Cognito still handles the sign-in step, SSO remains compatible with the other Hosted UI apps.</li>
                </ul>
            </article>
        </section>

        <section class="grid">
            <article class="panel">
                <h2>Session state</h2>
                <% if (isAuthenticated) { %>
                    <p>You are authenticated in this custom-login app. The session was created after your local page redirected the browser through Cognito and the callback returned here.</p>
                    <pre><%= JSON.stringify(userInfo, null, 2) %></pre>
                <% } else { %>
                    <p>No local session exists yet. Open the custom login page and continue to Cognito to begin the sign-in flow.</p>
                <% } %>
            </article>

            <article class="panel">
                <h2>Suggested demo flow</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li>Open the public page first to confirm that it works without authentication.</li>
                    <li>Open the protected page. The app should send you to the local custom login page.</li>
                    <li>Type a username hint if you want, then continue to Cognito.</li>
                    <li>If you already have a Cognito Hosted UI session from <span class="mono">app1</span> or <span class="mono">app2</span>, Cognito should bounce you back quickly.</li>
                    <li>After login, the app should return you to the protected page you originally requested.</li>
                </ol>
            </article>
        </section>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
